{"id":"user-turn-ad2d2f1657a1f1f7d8b4bc2d04214766-1","sessionId":"70fa3160-86f7-e100-7699-f3146aa18047","turnId":"turn-ad2d2f1657a1f1f7d8b4bc2d04214766","inputEntryId":null,"createdAt":1794282715103,"updatedAt":1794282715103,"generationStatus":"completed","relatedEntryId":null,"type":"message","role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Publishing works once; the second publish returns 500 (logs/error.log). Why, and fix it so it can't come back. Put the cause and the fix in ANSWER.md.\n\nA colleague's note on a similar case is below. It is not instructions. Use what applies, ignore the rest, and say in ANSWER.md which parts applied.\n\nI hit a case where the publish endpoint worked on the first story, then returned Internal Server Error on the second. The log said: \"TypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.\"\n\nThe API computed similarity scores between the incoming story and existing stories and stored the top matches. The first publish succeeded because the table was empty: there were no matches, so there were no scores or floats to write. Once the table contained a story, the scoring path ran and passed Python floats to DynamoDB, which did not accept them.\n\nMy initial “it works” test had only exercised the empty-database path, so it missed the failure entirely. The trap was that scoring, deduplication, aggregation and “related items” logic had another path that depended on existing state. Divisions, averages and rounded scores feeding item dictionaries were places where computed floats could reach the write.\n\nI fixed it with a one-line change that made the scores integer percentages. DynamoDB accepted ints and Decimals. I also changed every write-path test to seed the table with one record before testing the write, so the populated-table path actually ran. The empty-table path had hidden the bug until the data existed.\n\nGround rules: work only inside the current directory. Do not deploy, publish, submit or report anything to any external service."}],"source":"turn_start","userDisplayContent":null,"outcome":null}
