{"id":"assistant-77e397f7-ee5a-5d7a-ae77-d5678c9abe8e","sessionId":"70fa3160-86f7-e100-7699-f3146aa18047","turnId":"turn-ad2d2f1657a1f1f7d8b4bc2d04214766","inputEntryId":"user-turn-ad2d2f1657a1f1f7d8b4bc2d04214766-1","createdAt":1794282730923,"updatedAt":1794282730923,"generationStatus":"completed","relatedEntryId":null,"type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now let me fix the issue. The problem is clear:\n\n1. **Root cause**: The `similarity()` function returns a Python `float` (via `round()`), and this float is stored in the `similar` list in the item dictionary. When DynamoDB tries to serialize this, it fails because DynamoDB doesn't accept Python floats - it requires `Decimal` types.\n\n2. **Why it worked once**: The first publish had an empty table, so `related()` returned an empty list, meaning no scores were written. The second publish had existing stories, so `similarity()` was called and returned floats.\n\n3. **The fix**: Convert the similarity score to `Decimal` in the `related()` function where the scored items are created.\n\nLet me apply the fix:"}],"source":"harness","userDisplayContent":null,"outcome":{"type":"committed"}}
