{"id":"effect-8d241fd2-a50f-5a10-be8a-8360b0bfe545","sessionId":"70fa3160-86f7-e100-7699-f3146aa18047","turnId":"turn-ad2d2f1657a1f1f7d8b4bc2d04214766","inputEntryId":"user-turn-ad2d2f1657a1f1f7d8b4bc2d04214766-1","createdAt":1794282745664,"updatedAt":1794282745670,"generationStatus":"completed","relatedEntryId":null,"type":"effect","title":"vibe.todo","detail":{"toolName":"vibe.todo","display":{"summary":"Writing 4 todos","content":null,"suffix":"","verb":"Updating","message":"4 todos","settledVerb":"Updated","settledMessage":"4 todos","statusText":"Managing todos"},"kind":"todo","input":{"action":"write","todos":[{"id":"1","content":"Analyze the root cause from error.log and app.py","status":"completed","priority":"medium"},{"id":"2","content":"Fix the float issue in app.py by converting similarity scores to Decimal","status":"completed","priority":"medium"},{"id":"3","content":"Update test to seed table with existing story to catch the bug","status":"completed","priority":"medium"},{"id":"4","content":"Create ANSWER.md with cause and fix explanation","status":"in_progress","priority":"medium"}]}},"state":{"status":"completed","outputText":"{\"verb\": \"Updated\", \"todos\": [{\"id\": \"1\", \"content\": \"Analyze the root cause from error.log and app.py\", \"status\": \"completed\", \"priority\": \"medium\"}, {\"id\": \"2\", \"content\": \"Fix the float issue in app.py by converting similarity scores to Decimal\", \"status\": \"completed\", \"priority\": \"medium\"}, {\"id\": \"3\", \"content\": \"Update test to seed table with existing story to catch the bug\", \"status\": \"completed\", \"priority\": \"medium\"}, {\"id\": \"4\", \"content\": \"Create ANSWER.md with cause and fix explanation\", \"status\": \"in_progress\", \"priority\": \"medium\"}], \"total_count\": 4, \"message\": \"Updated 4 todos\"}","display":{"success":true,"verb":"Updated","message":"4 todos","warnings":[],"approvalNote":null,"suffix":""},"approvalSource":"bypass","decision":"execute","durationMs":0.0,"approvalType":"always","output":{"todos":[{"id":"1","content":"Analyze the root cause from error.log and app.py","status":"completed","priority":"medium"},{"id":"2","content":"Fix the float issue in app.py by converting similarity scores to Decimal","status":"completed","priority":"medium"},{"id":"3","content":"Update test to seed table with existing story to catch the bug","status":"completed","priority":"medium"},{"id":"4","content":"Create ANSWER.md with cause and fix explanation","status":"in_progress","priority":"medium"}]}}}
{"id":"effect-5db92242-5d33-5118-87e7-fa7306b0800f","sessionId":"70fa3160-86f7-e100-7699-f3146aa18047","turnId":"turn-ad2d2f1657a1f1f7d8b4bc2d04214766","inputEntryId":"user-turn-ad2d2f1657a1f1f7d8b4bc2d04214766-1","createdAt":1794282750190,"updatedAt":1794282750198,"generationStatus":"completed","relatedEntryId":null,"type":"effect","title":"file_system.write_file","detail":{"toolName":"file_system.write_file","display":{"summary":"Writing ANSWER.md","content":"# Root Cause and Fix\n\n## Cause\n\nThe `similarity()` function in `src/app.py` returns a Python `float` (via `round(..., 4)`). When a second story is published, the `related()` function computes similarity scores between the new story and existing stories, and these float values are placed into the `similar` list in the item dictionary. DynamoDB's boto3 serializer rejects Python float types with: `TypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.`\n\nThe first publish succeeded because the table was empty, so `related()` returned an empty list and no scores were written. Once a story existed, the scoring path executed and the float values triggered the error.\n\nThis matches the colleague's note: the empty-database path hid the bug, and the populated-table path exposed it when computed floats reached the write.\n\n## Fix\n\n1. **Code change in `src/app.py`:**\n   - Added `from decimal import Decimal` import\n   - In `related()`, wrapped the similarity score in `Decimal(str(similarity(story, other)))` so DynamoDB receives a valid Decimal type instead of a Python float\n\n2. **Test change in `tests/test_publish.py`:**\n   - Added `test_publish_with_existing_story` that seeds the table with one story before publishing a second, ensuring the populated-table path is tested\n\n## What from the colleague's note applied\n\n- The exact error message: \"TypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.\"\n- The pattern: first publish works (empty table), second fails (table has data)\n- The root cause: computed floats reaching DynamoDB writes\n- The fix strategy: convert floats to Decimal\n- The test gap: empty-table tests missed the bug; need to seed with existing data\n\nThe colleague's note was directly applicable to this case.\n","suffix":"","verb":"Creating","message":"ANSWER.md","settledVerb":"Created","settledMessage":"ANSWER.md","statusText":"Writing file"},"kind":"file_write","input":{"filePath":"ANSWER.md","content":"# Root Cause and Fix\n\n## Cause\n\nThe `similarity()` function in `src/app.py` returns a Python `float` (via `round(..., 4)`). When a second story is published, the `related()` function computes similarity scores between the new story and existing stories, and these float values are placed into the `similar` list in the item dictionary. DynamoDB's boto3 serializer rejects Python float types with: `TypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.`\n\nThe first publish succeeded because the table was empty, so `related()` returned an empty list and no scores were written. Once a story existed, the scoring path executed and the float values triggered the error.\n\nThis matches the colleague's note: the empty-database path hid the bug, and the populated-table path exposed it when computed floats reached the write.\n\n## Fix\n\n1. **Code change in `src/app.py`:**\n   - Added `from decimal import Decimal` import\n   - In `related()`, wrapped the similarity score in `Decimal(str(similarity(story, other)))` so DynamoDB receives a valid Decimal type instead of a Python float\n\n2. **Test change in `tests/test_publish.py`:**\n   - Added `test_publish_with_existing_story` that seeds the table with one story before publishing a second, ensuring the populated-table path is tested\n\n## What from the colleague's note applied\n\n- The exact error message: \"TypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.\"\n- The pattern: first publish works (empty table), second fails (table has data)\n- The root cause: computed floats reaching DynamoDB writes\n- The fix strategy: convert floats to Decimal\n- The test gap: empty-table tests missed the bug; need to seed with existing data\n\nThe colleague's note was directly applicable to this case.\n"}},"state":{"status":"completed","outputText":"","display":{"success":true,"verb":"Created","message":"ANSWER.md","warnings":[],"approvalNote":null,"suffix":""},"approvalSource":"bypass","decision":"execute","durationMs":0.0,"approvalType":"always","output":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/h-XJUKci/ANSWER.md","content":"# Root Cause and Fix\n\n## Cause\n\nThe `similarity()` function in `src/app.py` returns a Python `float` (via `round(..., 4)`). When a second story is published, the `related()` function computes similarity scores between the new story and existing stories, and these float values are placed into the `similar` list in the item dictionary. DynamoDB's boto3 serializer rejects Python float types with: `TypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.`\n\nThe first publish succeeded because the table was empty, so `related()` returned an empty list and no scores were written. Once a story existed, the scoring path executed and the float values triggered the error.\n\nThis matches the colleague's note: the empty-database path hid the bug, and the populated-table path exposed it when computed floats reached the write.\n\n## Fix\n\n1. **Code change in `src/app.py`:**\n   - Added `from decimal import Decimal` import\n   - In `related()`, wrapped the similarity score in `Decimal(str(similarity(story, other)))` so DynamoDB receives a valid Decimal type instead of a Python float\n\n2. **Test change in `tests/test_publish.py`:**\n   - Added `test_publish_with_existing_story` that seeds the table with one story before publishing a second, ensuring the populated-table path is tested\n\n## What from the colleague's note applied\n\n- The exact error message: \"TypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.\"\n- The pattern: first publish works (empty table), second fails (table has data)\n- The root cause: computed floats reaching DynamoDB writes\n- The fix strategy: convert floats to Decimal\n- The test gap: empty-table tests missed the bug; need to seed with existing data\n\nThe colleague's note was directly applicable to this case.\n","fileExisted":false,"previousContent":null}}}
