{"id":"assistant-1a778fcc-3d74-5cfd-866a-22bf3a290e35","sessionId":"70fa3160-86f7-e100-7699-f3146aa18047","turnId":"turn-ad2d2f1657a1f1f7d8b4bc2d04214766","inputEntryId":"user-turn-ad2d2f1657a1f1f7d8b4bc2d04214766-1","createdAt":1794282754589,"updatedAt":1794282754589,"generationStatus":"completed","relatedEntryId":null,"type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Here's the summary:\n\n**Root cause:** The `similarity()` function returns a Python `float`, which DynamoDB rejects. The first publish worked because the table was empty (no scores computed). The second publish failed because existing stories triggered the scoring path, and the float values in the `similar` list caused `TypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.`\n\n**Fix applied:**\n1. Added `from decimal import Decimal` to `src/app.py`\n2. Changed `related()` to wrap scores: `Decimal(str(similarity(story, other)))` instead of raw float\n3. Added `test_publish_with_existing_story` test that seeds the table first\n\n**Files changed:**\n- `src/app.py` - Added Decimal import and conversion\n- `tests/test_publish.py` - Added test for populated-table path\n- `ANSWER.md` - Created with cause, fix, and note on what applied from the colleague's note\n\nAll tests pass. The bug cannot return because floats are now converted to Decimal before reaching DynamoDB."}],"source":"harness","userDisplayContent":null,"outcome":{"type":"committed"}}
